course: dictionary
lesson: 11049
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is right. A wedge can be a piece of wood or metal that is thick at one end and thin at the other, a slice of cheese or lemon, or a verb meaning to push something into a tight space. «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay, making wedge-shaped marks.» Here wedge-shaped means shaped like a wedge, so the shape is part of the meaning.
explain: Look at the words around it to find out whether wedge is a thing or an action. «Wedge the door open so the cat can get in.» Wedge is a doing word here, because you are holding the door in place with something. The word open tells you that the door must stay still.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The bag was wedged under the bench, so it could not slide.» Wedged means pushed into a tight space so it stayed there, and that fits. If your meaning makes no sense, try another one, like a slice or a tool, until the sentence works.
fact: A wedge is thick at one end and thin at the other.
fact: As a noun, a wedge can be a tool, such as a door wedge or an axe head, or a slice, such as a wedge of cheese or lemon.
fact: As a verb, to wedge means to push or squeeze something into a tight space so it stays there.
fact: In science, a wedge is one of the simple machines, used in axes and knives to split things.
fact: «Cuneiform» means wedge-shaped, the marks scribes pressed into wet clay.
exercise: «Wedge the door open so the cat can get in.» What does wedge mean here? | To count the cats | *To hold something in place with a wedge | To sing very loudly | To paint something bright red
exercise: «A wedge, like an axe head or a door stop, is a ramp that turns one downward blow into strong sideways pushes.» Which everyday thing is a wedge? | A window made of glass | A bowl of soup | A soft feather pillow | *An axe head
exercise: «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay, making wedge-shaped marks called cuneiform.» What does wedge-shaped mean? | Round like a ball | Soft and wet | Made of gold | *Thick at one end and thin at the other
test: «He wedged his bag under the bench.» What does wedged mean here? | Lost forever | Lifted high in the air | *Pushed into a tight space so it stayed there | Washed
test: «Dad cut the lemon and put a wedge on each plate.» What is a wedge in this sentence? | *A slice of lemon | A sharp knife | A tool for splitting wood | A cloud of steam
exam: «The cat wedged itself under the sofa.» What kind of word is wedged here? | A pronoun, a word like it or she | *A verb, a doing word | A noun, a naming word | An adjective, a describing word
